If a LoginFactoryTalk... method has not been explicitly called to establish the desired user for
download operations, this method will implicitly log in the current user which will display a
login dialog if Single Sign-On (SSO) is not enabled.
This snippet shows how to use the  method to begin a download of a project to a particular controller.

var client = ClientFactory.GetServiceApiClientV1("My App Name");
var chassisGuid = (await client.ListChassis()).First().ChassisGuid;
var controllerGuid = (await client.ListControllers(chassisGuid)).First().ControllerGuid;
var acdPath = "C:\\users\\username\\projects\\project.ACD";
using (var fileHandle = await client.SendFile(acdPath))
{
    await client.Download(controllerGuid, fileHandle); // only begins download operation
}

This snippet shows how to use the  method to cancel a download in progress.

var client = ClientFactory.GetServiceApiClientV1("My App Name");
var chassisGuid = (await client.ListChassis()).First().ChassisGuid;
var controllerGuid = (await client.ListControllers(chassisGuid)).First().ControllerGuid;
var acdPath = "C:\\users\\username\\projects\\project.ACD";
using (var fileHandle = await client.SendFile(acdPath))
{
