            This method will cause any associated controllers to be reset. Controller configuration will remain, but any
            project contained on the controller will be removed and the controller will be restarted.



            The address parameter is used when the replace operation will cause one of the following scenarios:


The target controller will lose one of its IP address configurations because it is going from Dual IP to DLR mode.

The target controller will lose one of its IP address configurations because it is going from Dual IP mode to a controller whose firmware does not support mutliple IP addresses.

            In either of these cases, the Service needs to know which of the two available IP configurations to use, and will discard the other.
            If the address is left null or set to  (0.0.0.0), it will be treated as a default and the
            secondary IP configuration of the controller will be used, with the primary discarded. If the IP address provided is not one currently
            set on the target controller, an exception will be thrown. This parameter is not intended to set a new IP address on the target controller.

